infographic hierarchy-tree-curved-line-rounded-rect-node
data
  title Declare, don't build: the four payoffs of DI
  desc One shift — constructor-declared dependencies, injected by the IoC container — buys these four
  root
    label DI: declare what you need
    children
      - label Testability
        desc overrideProvider swaps in a mock, so the consumer runs with no real database and no network.
      - label Single source of wiring
        desc Construction is described once in module metadata, not scattered — adding a dependency is a one-line constructor edit.
      - label Loose coupling
        desc Consumers depend on what a provider does, not how it's built — swap caching, logging, or a new impl behind the same token.
      - label Lifecycle management
        desc The container owns each provider's lifetime — singleton by default — and drives onModuleInit / onApplicationShutdown in dependency order.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
